.TH smi-project-prepare "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset 0.156.0" "SMI Project Command"
.SH NAME
smi-project-prepare \- start a new private project from a public template repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-project-prepare
\fINEW_PROJECT_NAME\fR \fITEMPLATE_REPO_URL\fR \fIPRIVATE_REPOS_DIR\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBsmi-project-prepare\fR command makes a new private, closed source project from a public
template repository, and protects the template from an accidental push of the private code.
.PP
When run, it performs the following:
.IP \[bu] 2
Creates the bare repository \fIPRIVATE_REPOS_DIR\fR/\fINEW_PROJECT_NAME\fR.git with the initial
branch \fBmaster\fR on the private repository host, over ssh.
.IP \[bu] 2
Clones the \fBmaster\fR branch of \fITEMPLATE_REPO_URL\fR into ./\fINEW_PROJECT_NAME\fR of the current
directory, with the template as the remote \fBupstream\fR.
.IP \[bu] 2
Adds the private repository as the remote \fBorigin\fR, and makes it the default push target with
.B remote.pushDefault
and
.BR "push.default simple" .
.IP \[bu] 2
Sets the push URL of \fBupstream\fR to \fBDISABLED\fR, so a push to the template fails. Fetching from
the template still works, so its later changes can be merged into the new project.
.IP \[bu] 2
Pushes \fBmaster\fR to \fBorigin\fR and sets it as the upstream branch, then prints the remotes, the
branches and the local Git configuration.
.PP
The command fails if an argument is missing, if \fBSMI_PRIVATE_REPO_HOST\fR is not set or is a URL or
path instead of a host, if the project name is empty, has a slash or starts with a dot, or if
\&./\fINEW_PROJECT_NAME\fR already exists.
.PP
The template code is left as it is. A cleanup of the copy, such as \fBsmi-project-cleanup\fR of the
Spring Boot template app, is a separate step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fINEW_PROJECT_NAME\fR
Name of the new project: the local folder and the name of the private repository.
.TP
\fITEMPLATE_REPO_URL\fR
Git URL of the template repository the new project starts from.
.TP
\fIPRIVATE_REPOS_DIR\fR
Folder of the bare repositories on the private repository host.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_PRIVATE_REPO_HOST
Private repository host, [\fIuser\fR@]\fIhost\fR, required. There is no default.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Make ./myproject from the setmy.info template, with the origin
git.example.com:/srv/git/projects/myproject.git:
.PP
.B SMI_PRIVATE_REPO_HOST=git.example.com smi-project-prepare myproject git@github.com:setmy-info/setmy.info.git /srv/git/projects
